hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1325","Al-Hussein bin Issa Al-Bistami narrated to us, Muhammad bin Abi Fudaik Al-Madani narrated to us, on the authority of Kathir bin Zayd, on the authority of Al-Muttalib bin Hantab, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “If one of you enters the mosque, he should not sit down until he has kneeled two rak’ahs.” Abu Bakr said: This is a long chapter that I included in the book of Al-Kabir. Abu Bakr said: This matter is a matter of virtue, not an obligation, and the evidence for that is the news of Talha bin Abdullah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him. When he mentioned the five daily prayers, the man said: Do I have to do anything else? He said: No, unless you do it voluntarily, then know that anything other than the five prayers is voluntary and not obligatory."
